{"name":"Patina","hex":"#66d0c0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"patina","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A paten (a flat type of dish).","The colour or incrustation which age and wear give to (chiefly metallic) objects; especially, the green rust which covers works of art such as ancient bronzes, coins and medals."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green colour, tinted with grey, like that of bronze patina."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patina"}],"entries":[{"title":"Patina","blocks":[{"text":"Patina is a thin layer that variously forms on the surface of copper, brass, bronze, and similar metals and alloys, or certain stones and wooden furniture, or any similar acquired change of a surface through age and exposure."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Minneapolis_City_Hall.jpg/330px-Minneapolis_City_Hall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patina","wikidata":"Q428352"},{"title":"Patina (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Patina is a young adult novel by Jason Reynolds, published August 29, 2017 by Atheneum. It is the second book in Reynold's Track series, preceded by Ghost (2016) and followed by Sunny (2018) and Lu (2018)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b4/Patina_-_Jason_Reynolds_book.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patina_(novel)","wikidata":"Q110577027"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/FraunkircheSouth.jpg/500px-FraunkircheSouth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/FraunkircheSouth.jpg/1280px-FraunkircheSouth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/